Now compute_hit_miss helper (pure, tested):

```rust
pub(crate) fn compute_hit_miss(predicted: &[String], changed: &[String]) -> HitMiss {
    let predicted_set: HashSet<&str> = predicted.iter().map(|s| s.as_str()).collect();
    let changed_set: HashSet<&str> = changed.iter().map(|s| s.as_str()).collect();
    let mut hits = Vec::new();
    let mut missed_predictions = Vec::new();
    let mut unpredicted_changes = Vec::new();
    for p in predicted {
        if changed_set.contains(p.as_str()) {
            hits.push(p.clone());
        } else {
            missed_predictions.push(p.clone());
        }
    }
    for c in changed {
        if !predicted_set.contains(c.as_str()) {
            unpredicted_changes.push(c.clone());
        }
    }
    // deterministic ordering: keep input orders (predicted order, changed order)
    HitMiss { hits, missed_predictions, unpredicted_changes }
}
```

Note: the dedupe — a file can't be in both hits and missed_predictions. And unpredicted_changes excludes hits. Good.

